# scenarios/5_loan.books: loaded by ledger_server into 5_loan.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	5. A loan: borrowing is not income, interest is a cost
about	The bank's 10,000 is owed back (Loans, a liability), so it is no revenue, and repaying it is no cost: only the interest is. The van it buys is an asset, worth a fifth less each year.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	173000	liability	Loans
account	240000	asset	Furniture
account	650000	expense	Interest
account	630000	expense	Depreciation
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Capital	-200000
posting	Bank account	200000
entry	2011-01-10	The bank lends 10,000
posting	Loans	-1000000
posting	Bank account	1000000
entry	2011-01-15	A delivery van for 8,000
posting	Bank account	-800000
posting	Furniture	800000
entry	2011-06-30	1,000 of the loan is repaid
posting	Bank account	-100000
posting	Loans	100000
entry	2011-06-30	Interest on the loan for six months
posting	Bank account	-30000
posting	Interest	30000
entry	2011-12-31	1,000 of the loan is repaid
posting	Bank account	-100000
posting	Loans	100000
entry	2011-12-31	Interest on the loan for six months
posting	Bank account	-27000
posting	Interest	27000
entry	2011-12-31	The van loses a fifth of its value to depreciation
posting	Furniture	-160000
posting	Depreciation	160000
